\n\nFor your protection and privacy, please press the Clear This Form button after you have printed the form.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAnswer—Disability Access | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/jcc-form/DAL-002)\nciteturn1658search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; # Answer—Disability Access (DAL-002)Tell the court and the other side that you do not agree with what was said in a letter or court complaint claiming that a building that you own or in which you are a tenant does not meet requirements for access of disabled persons and also tell them reasons you are not legally responsible (liable) for things the letter or complaint claims.\n\n# Answer—Disability Access (DAL-002)\n\nTell the court and the other side that you do not agree with what was said in a letter or court complaint claiming that a building that you own or in which you are a tenant does not meet requirements for access of disabled persons and also tell them reasons you are not legally responsible (liable) for things the letter or complaint claims.\n\nGet form DAL-002\n\nEffective: July 1, 2016--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJUDICIAL COUNCIL OF CALIFORNIA (https://www.courts.ca.gov/documents/W16-03.pdf)\nciteturn1658search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.0 years ago; DAL-002 ...  | FOR COURT USE ONLY ... www.courts.ca.gov\nDAL-002\n | DAL-002\n--- | ---\n | FOR COURT USE ONLY\nSUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF\nSTREET ADDRESS:\nMAILING ADDRESS:\nCITY: ZIP CODE:\nBRANCH NAME:  | \nPlaintiff:\nDefendant:  | \nANSWER—DISABILITY ACCESS  | CASE NUMBER:This form may be filed with the court and served on the plaintiff as an answer to the complaint, or it may be used as an informal \nresponse to a demand letter or for settlement discussion purposes.\n1.   \nDefendant(s) (Each defendant for whom this answer is filed must be named and must sign this answer unless his or her attorney \nsigns):           \nanswers the complaint as follows: \n2.   Check ONLY ONE of the next three boxes, a, b, or c:\na.\nDefendant generally denies each statement of the complaint.\nb.\nDefendant denies that plaintiff has demonstrated that he or she was denied full and equal access to the place of public \naccommodation on a particular occasion. (See Civil Code section 55.56.)\nDefendant admits that all of the statements of the complaint are true EXCEPT:\nc.\n(1)\nDefendant claims the following statements of the complaint are false.  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nItem number: (https://beta.courts.ca.gov/system/files/file/rupro-20160318-materials.pdf)\nciteturn1658search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.4 years ago; DAL-002\nDAL-002\nCASE NUMBER:\nPLAINTIFF:\nDEFENDANT:\n4.\nFACTS SUPPORTING AFFIRMATIVE DEFENSES (NOTE: For each box checked in item 3, you must state brief facts to support \nthe defense. Include letters a, b, c, and d from item 3 to make clear which affirmative defense(s) you are supporting.)\n Supporting facts are on Attachment 4. (You may use form MC-025 for this purpose.)\n5.\nA request for an early evaluation conference and to meet in person with plaintiff at the subject premises has been filed or is \nbeing filed concurrently with this answer, on Defendant's Application for Stay of Proceedings and Early Evaluation \nConference, Joint Inspection (form DAL-005).\n6.\nDefendant qualifies for reduced damages. (See Civ. Code, § 55.56(f)(1) or (2).)\nNumber of pages attached:\n7.\n(Each defendant for whom this answer is filed must be named in item 1 and must sign this answer unless his or her attorney signs.)\n(TYPE OR PRINT NAME)\n(SIGNATURE OF DEFENDANT OR ATTORNEY)\n(TYPE OR PRINT NAME)\n(SIGNATURE OF DEFENDANT OR ATTORNEY)\nVERIFICATION\n(Use a different verification form if the verification is by an attorney or for a corporation or partnership.)\nI am the defendant in this proceeding and have read this answer. I declare under penalty of perjury under the laws of the State of  \nCalifornia that the foregoing is true and correct.\nDate:\n(TYPE OR PRINT NAME)\n(SIGNATURE OF DEFENDANT)\nANSWER—DISABILITY ACCESS\nDAL-002 [New July 1, 2016]\nPage 2 of 2\n10--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDAL-002\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n<tr>\n<td>ATTORNEY OR PART (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files/file/rupro-20160318-materials.pdf)\nciteturn1658search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10.6 years ago; Crawled: 10.5 years ago; DAL-002 ... <td>FOR COURT USE ONLY<br><br>DRAFT<br>03/08/16<br><br>NOT APPROVED<br>BY JUDICIAL<br>COUNCIL</td> ... www.courts.ca.gov\nDAL-002\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n<tr>\n<td>ATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY:<br>NAME:<br>FIRM NAME:<br>STREET ADDRESS:<br>CITY:<br>TELEPHONE NO.:<br>E-MAIL ADDRESS:<br>ATTORNEY FOR (name):</td>\n<td>STATE BAR NO.:<br>STATE:<br>ZIP CODE:<br>FAX NO.:</td>\n<td>FOR COURT USE ONLY<br><br>DRAFT<br>03/08/16<br><br>NOT APPROVED<br>BY JUDICIAL<br>COUNCIL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>SUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF</b><br>STREET ADDRESS:<br>MAILING ADDRESS:<br>CITY AND ZIP CODE:<br>BRANCH NAME:</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PLAINTIFF:<br>DEFENDANT:</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>ANSWER—DISABILITY ACCESS</b></td>\n<td>CASE NUMBER:</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\nThis form may be filed with the court and served on the plaintiff as an answer to the complaint, or it may be used as an informal response to a demand letter or for settlement discussion purposes.\n\n1. Defendant(s) (Each defendant for whom this answer is filed must be named and must sign this answer unless his or her attorney signs):\n\nanswers the complaint as follows:\n\n2. <b>Check ONLY ONE of the next three boxes, a, b, or c:</b>  \na. ☐ Defendant generally denies each statement of the complaint.  \nb. ☐ Defendant denies that plaintiff has demonstrated that he or she was denied full and equal access to the place of public accommodation on a particular occasion. (See Civ. Code, § 55.56.)  \nc. ☐ Defendant admits that all of the statements of the complaint are true EXCEPT:\n\n(1) Defendant claims the following statements of the complaint are false. <i>(State paragraph numbers from the complaint or explain below.)</i> ☐ Explanation is on Attachment 2c(1). <i>(You may use form MC-025 for this purpose.)</i>\n\n(2) Defendant has no information or belief that the following statements of the complaint are true, so defendant denies them. <i>(State paragraph numbers from the complaint or explain below.)</i>  \n☐ Explanation is on Attachment 2c(2). <i>(You may use form MC-025 for this purpose.)</i>\n\n3. AFFIRMATIVE DEFENSES <i>(NOTE: For each box checked below, you must state brief facts to support it in item 4.)</i>  \na. ☐ Defendant is not liable because the facility is not open to the public.  \nb. ☐ Defendant is not liable because defendant's landlord is responsible for ensuring that some or all of the property leased by the defendant, including the areas at issue in the complaint, are accessible to the public. <i>(Give the name and contact information of defendant's landlord in item 4.)</i>  \nc. ☐ Other affirmative defenses. <i>(Specify and state facts in support in item 4.)</i>\n\nPage 1 of 2\n\nForm Approved for Optional Use  \nJudicial Council of California  \nDAL-002 [New July 1, 2016]\n\nANSWER—DISABILITY ACCESS\n\nCivil Code, § 55.56  \nwww.courts.ca.gov\n\n9--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJUDICIAL COUNCIL FORMS (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files?file=rules-court%2Fappendix_0.pdf)\nciteturn1658search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; | DAL-002 | 7/1/2016 | Answer—Disability Access |  |\nJUDICIAL COUNCIL FORMS\n\n| Form number | Effective date | Form title | [Rev. July 21, 2026] |\n|---|---:|---|---|\n| DAL-001 V | 10/23/2009 | Important Information for Building Owners a